exp_map = {
    "For the acryloylation of a phenolic amine (entry 17948) the base was changed from TEA to 2,6-lutidine and the acyl chloride feed was slowed. Impurity S-17 dropped from 12 % to < 1 % and overall isolated yield increased from 68 % to 85 %.": ["change_base", "slow_addition_feed"],
    "A factorial DoE varied H₂O₂ (2-6 equiv) and LiOH (1.2-2.0 equiv) while monitoring hydroxy-amide impurity by HPLC. The optimum (4.6 equiv H₂O₂, 1.6 equiv LiOH) gave > 99 % conversion with <= 5 % impurity (16793).": ["change_oxidant","change_base", "factorial_doe"],
    "Run a temperature-profile study (30 °C -> 70 °C) while holding reagent equivalents constant. Identify the temperature where impurity formation begins (e.g., > 0.25 % enantiomer). Implement a controlled ramp or operate at the lower temperature with a slight excess of electrophile to maintain conversion. Validate on a pilot-scale batch with in-process HPLC.": ["temperature_profile_study", "change_equivalents", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A systematic base-screen (LiO-t-Bu, NaOt-Bu, Cs₂CO₃.2 H₂O) was conducted for the silanol coupling (entry 10876). NaOt-Bu reduced protodesilylation from 35 % to < 5 % and increased product yield from 42 % to 78 %. Parallel addition of 0.05 equiv CuI further suppressed dimer formation in the Barluenga reaction (entry 3933).": ["change_base", "factorial_doe", "parallel_addition_catalyst"],
    "Introduce a dedicated Pd-scavenging step (e.g., N-acetyl-cysteine aqueous wash, polymer-bound scavenger, metal-chelating resin) and verify removal by ICP-OES; alternatively redesign the sequence to avoid Pd-containing intermediates (telescoping, in-line quench).": ["introduce_scavenging_step", "telescoping", "change_workup"],
    "A DoE varying K₂HPO₄ concentration and KOH addition was performed on a 20 L batch. The optimal condition (pH 9 ± 0.2) reduced impurity 34 from 9 % to <0.2 % while maintaining >99 % conversion.": ["factorial_doe", "change_base"],
    "Run a series of small-scale trials varying (i) amine equivalents (0.9 -> 1.2 eq), (ii) base identity (triethylamine, DIPEA, potassium carbonate), and (iii) addition order (base -> acid -> amine vs. simultaneous). Analyze impurity levels by LC-MS. Scale the optimal condition to pilot batch and confirm impurity suppression.": ["change_equivalents", "change_base", "addition_order_study", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A DoE varying base (LiOH vs. NaOH/KOH), temperature (0 °C -> 25 °C), and solvent (MeOH, EtOH, DMF) showed that LiOH in MeOH at 0 °C suppressed bis-acid formation to < 0.1 % and eliminated N-alkylation. The optimal stoichiometry (2 equiv LiOH) was then fixed for scale-up.": ["factorial_doe", "change_base", "temperature_profile_study", "change_solvent", "change_equivalents"],
    "A step-wise addition study where the acyl chloride (or benzoyl chloride) was fed in three portions (0.8 eq -> 1.2 eq -> 0.4 eq) while monitoring impurity formation by in-line IR. Parallel runs compared DMF (high polarity) vs toluene (low polarity) as solvent, and evaluated the effect of adding a catalytic amount of tetrabutylammonium-hydrogensulfate. Impurity levels were quantified after work-up.": ["addition_order_study", "change_equivalents", "change_solvent", "in_line_monitoring"],
    "A fed-batch experiment on the KRED-119 kinetic resolution (entry 17424) compared three strategies: (i) no pH control, (ii) manual addition of Na₂CO₃ every hour, (iii) automated pH-feedback loop dosing 2 M Na₂CO₃. Strategy iii kept pH 6.8 ± 0.1 unit and restored full conversion (>99 %) whereas the uncontrolled run stalled at 45 % conversion after 30 min.": ["addition_order_study"],
    "* Conduct a temperature-ramp study (120 °C -> 200 °C, 10 °C increments) while keeping residence time constant.  * Quantify impurity levels (e.g., impurity D, hemiaminal, urea) at each temperature.  * Test the addition of a mild base (2,6-lutidine) or an additive (ascorbic acid) to suppress oxidation.  * Choose the lowest temperature that still gives >= 95 % conversion with impurity < 0.1 %.": ["temperature_profile_study", "change_base", "change_additive", "in_line_monitoring"],
    "* Conduct time-course studies (6, 12, 18, 24 h) at 130 °C for the DCQ + HNDA SNAr, monitoring impurity profile by qNMR.  * Identify the time where conversion plateaus (~99 %) and stop the reaction.  * Validate on 5 kg batch with in-process sampling; compare impurity levels to a 48 h run.": ["time_course_study", "pilot_scale_validation", "in_line_monitoring"],
    "A factorial DoE varied base (K₂CO₃ vs. DIPEA), additive (TBAC, Ca-propionate), and nucleophile excess (1.0-1.5 eq). The optimal condition used DIPEA (1.0 eq) with TBAC (0.5 eq) and 1.1 eq nucleophile, which reduced the bis-alkylated impurity from 12 % to <0.5 % on a 100 kg scale.":
    ["factorial_doe", "change_base", "parallel_addition_catalyst", "change_equivalents"],
    "For the CuI/TEMPO system, the support was changed from γ-Al₂O₃ to mesoporous alumina, and the O₂ feed was reduced to 5 % in N₂. After a 150 h run, the aldehyde yield remained > 90 % without the earlier decline observed with the original catalyst.": ["change_catalyst_support", "change_equivalents", "long_term_stability_test"],
    "A regeneration protocol (oxidative burn-off at 350 °C) was applied to spent Pd/C after four cycles; activity was restored to > 95 % of the fresh catalyst. Parallel runs with a more stable Pd/alumina catalyst showed no activity loss over ten cycles, allowing a 30 % reduction in catalyst inventory.": ["catalyst_regeneration", "change_catalyst_support", "long_term_stability_test"],
    "Perform impurity profiling of raw materials (e.g., sulfur content by elemental analysis); if impurity present, add a scavenger (N-acetyl-cysteine) or switch to a cleaner reagent (e.g., use aryl chloride instead of bromide that carries less sulfur); adjust Pd loading based on impurity level.": ["introduce_scavenging_step", "change_substrate", "change_equivalents"],
    "A side-by-side comparison of 10 % Pd/C (dry) vs. 10 % Pd(OH)₂/Al₂O₃ (500 µm) in a continuous-flow packed-bed. Pressure-drop monitoring showed a stable ΔP of 0.8 bar for the alumina-supported catalyst versus a rising ΔP up to 3.5 bar for dry Pd/C after 4 h. No fouling observed with the alumina catalyst.": ["change_catalyst_support", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "long_term_stability_test"],
    "A comparative study on Na-selectride reductions (entry 8375) screened three commercial batches of Na-selectride. Batch A gave dr = 20:1, batch B gave dr = 1:1. The low-dr batch was replaced with K-selectride (same stoichiometry) and the reaction was re-run, achieving dr = 5:1 and >90 % isolated yield. For the KRED-9 packed-bed (entry 14560), switching from CEP to LX1000HA beads eliminated back-pressure and maintained >99 % conversion over 64 h continuous operation.": ["change_catalyst_support", "long_term_stability_test"],
    '* Conduct a DoE screening of acid sources (4 M MeOH HCl, 5 M EtOH HCl, 4 N HCl in dioxane, aqueous 4 M HCl) at a fixed substrate loading.  * For each source, measure the residual Boc-protected material after a fixed reaction time (2 h, 50 °C).  * Include a "fresh-titrate" control where the HCl solution is titrated with a base just before dosing.  * Select the acid that gives >= 98 % deprotection with the lowest excess.': ["factorial_doe", "change_acid", "fresh_titrate_control"],
    '* Run a systematic DoE varying catalyst loading (0.05 % -> 0.5 % wt) and measure conversion after a fixed residence time.  * Perform ICP-MS on spent catalyst to quantify metal leaching; correlate with activity loss.  * Introduce a short "pre-conditioning" run (e.g., 5 min at high temperature) before each production batch to regenerate the catalyst surface.': ["factorial_doe", "catalyst_regeneration", "change_equivalents"],
    "Compare three catalyst systems (G2, SG, Hoveyda-Grubbs II) at 1 mol % and 2.5 mol % loadings in parallel reactors; monitor dimer formation by LC-MS and residual Ru by ICP-MS. Introduce a post-reaction quench with ethyl-vinyl-ether or a silica-bound thiol scavenger in a subset to evaluate impurity suppression.": ["change_catalyst", "change_equivalents", "introduce_scavenging_step", "in_line_monitoring"],
    "A custom 3-D-printed Y-mixer with enlarged outlet diameter (0.25 in) and Hastelloy construction was fabricated. The process was run with a high-velocity THF rinse (10 L min⁻¹) after each batch. Clogging events dropped from 4 per 10 batches to 0, and overall isolated yield increased from 71 % to 61 % crude assay.": ["change_mixer_design", "introduce_cleaning_protocol", "long_term_stability_test"],
    "A scale-up trial added 20 % v/v MeOH to the hydrolysate before filtration and employed a 10 µm mesh filter downstream of the reactor. Filtration time dropped from > 2 h to < 30 min, and no fouling was observed over multiple batches (17256).": ["change_solvent", "change_filtration_method", "long_term_stability_test"],
    "A pilot-scale flow of the Cu-catalysed amination (aryl bromide + amine) was run in 3 mm ID tubing with a vented BPR (1 bar). Parallel runs compared (a) original 10 mm ID tubing, (b) 7.94 mm ID tubing, and (c) 7.94 mm ID plus an inline ultrasonic bath. Only the ultrasonic-assisted run avoided blockage; pressure remained <=0.8 bar throughout 10 h operation.": ["change_tubing_diameter", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "ultrasonic_assistance", "long_term_stability_test"],
    "Test alternative solvents/co-solvents that keep all reagents in solution (e.g., replace 1,4-dioxane with 2-MeTHF, add ethylene glycol to BBA, switch THF -> toluene for aryl chlorides); evaluate filtration or inline solids-removal devices.": ["change_solvent", "change_substrate", "change_filtration_method"],
    "Compare three reactor configurations: (i) standard PFA tubing (1 mm ID), (ii) larger-ID tubing (2 mm), and (iii) a custom V-shaped static mixer. Run the same reaction at identical residence time while monitoring pressure, flow rate, and product quality. Select the configuration that eliminates pressure excursions and maintains conversion.": ["change_reactor_configuration", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "in_line_monitoring"],
    "A solubility screening DoE was performed for the problematic substrate (e.g., azelaic acid, pinacol boronic ester) in binary solvent systems (MeOH/MeCN, MeOH/MTBE, MeOH/2-MeTHF) at 25 °C, 40 °C, and 60 °C. The highest single-phase concentration that remained clear for >=4 h was selected for scale-up. In flow, a 0.5 % w/w surfactant (Pluronic F-127) was added to the feed to keep particles suspended, and pressure-drop monitoring was used to verify clog-free operation.": ["factorial_doe", "change_solvent", "change_additive", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "long_term_stability_test"],
    "* Compare pressure profiles for 100 µm vs 200 µm Pd/C in identical column dimensions.  * Conduct CFD simulations of gas-liquid flow in a micropacked-bed to identify optimal particle-to-tube diameter ratios.  * Test a staged-bed configuration (coarse upstream, fine downstream) to balance conversion and pressure drop.": ["change_particle_size", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "kinetic_modeling", "change_reactor_configuration"],
    "For the benzylic chloride 2 (entries 10504/10503) performed precipitation at 0 °C with water as antisolvent and reduced the reaction temperature to 0 °C during work-up, preventing hydrolysis. Replaced SOCl₂ with POCl₃ for the quinazoline chlorination (entries 21347/21350) and limited POCl₃ to 2 equiv, which eliminated the need for >20 equiv and reduced impurity formation. Conducted a time-course study showing >90 % stability of the chloro-oxime when kept at <=20 °C in DMF.": ["change_workup", "change_oxidant", "change_equivalents", "time_course_study"],
    "Introduce a small inline filter (e.g., 50 µm mesh) upstream of the reactor and compare pressure profiles with and without a co-solvent that solubilises the solid (e.g., adding MeOH to a THF-based slurry). Record the time to blockage at pilot scale.": ["change_filtration_method", "change_solvent", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "long_term_stability_test"],
    "- Replace the aqueous work-up with a MeCN-water mixture (4:1) that precipitates the product and collapses the emulsion (as in entry 7415).  - Add a brine wash or a small amount of sodium chloride to increase ionic strength and break the emulsion.  - Test alternative quench agents (NaOH instead of KOH) that give cleaner phase splits (entry 21194).  - Verify recovery by measuring product concentration in both phases after separation.": ["change_workup", "change_solvent", "in_line_monitoring"],
    "Screen alternative aqueous/organic solvent systems (e.g., TPGS-750-M + acetone, TL-82 surfactant blend, THF -> toluene) and/or add a low-viscosity cosolvent; evaluate mixing hardware (high-shear homogenizer, overhead stirrer) and quantify phase-clearance time.": ["change_solvent", "change_additive", "change_mixer_design", "in_line_monitoring"],
    "Run a series of small-scale extractions varying pH (e.g., NaHCO₃ 0.1 M vs. 0.5 M) and organic solvent (EtOAc, MTBE, 1-octanol). Measure phase-breakup time and product distribution. Implement the optimal pH/solvent combo in a pilot-scale continuous extractor and monitor phase disengagement.": ["change_solvent", "change_additive", "change_extraction_method", "in_line_monitoring"],
    "Conduct a virtual DoE (or actual DoE) varying bromide equivalents from 1.0 to 1.5 eq and base equivalents from 1.0 to 2.0 eq. Track conversion, impurity profile, and material cost. Select the minimal excess that still delivers > 98 % conversion. Where possible, replace expensive bases (e.g., Cs₂CO₃) with K₂CO₃ or Na₂CO₃, and replace costly PTCs with catalytic TBAB.": ["factorial_doe", "change_equivalents", "change_base", "change_additive"],
    "Screen a set of antisolvents (e.g., IPA, EtOAc, MeCN) and temperatures (0 -> 25 °C) to identify conditions that produce a free-flowing crystalline solid. Perform a small-scale filtration test to measure cake permeability and moisture content. Implement the optimal quench/solvent system at pilot scale and compare filtration time and product recovery.": ["change_solvent", "change_workup", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "long_term_stability_test"],
    "The lithium carboxylate was replaced by the sodium analogue (entry 17787) and the acyl chloride was pre-dissolved in 10 % acetonitrile before addition (entry 8430). In a 500 L batch the slurry disappeared, pump pressure stayed constant and overall yield improved from 78 % to 92 %.": ["change_substrate", "change_solvent", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "long_term_stability_test"],
    "* Perform a solvent-swap study: after deprotection, dilute the reaction mixture with EtOAc, MeCN, or isopropanol, then add a non-solvent (heptane, MTBE, isopropyl ether) in varying ratios.  * Measure particle size distribution (laser diffraction) and filtration rate (pressure drop).  * Identify the antisolvent volume that yields a filterable cake with >= 90 % recovery.  * Validate the chosen crystallisation/filtration protocol on a pilot-scale batch.": ["change_solvent", "change_workup", "change_additive", "in_line_monitoring", "long_term_stability_test"],
    "* Run a comparative batch electrolysis at 0.5 mmol scale using TMG, NaOMe, and KOPiv as bases; monitor voltage vs. time.  * Implement a cleaning protocol (10 % aq. HCl rinse) after each 8 h run on a 5 kg loop.  * Test alternative anode material (Ir/Ta-MOX) for durability over 100 h continuous operation.": ["change_base", "introduce_cleaning_protocol", "change_anode_material", "long_term_stability_test"],
    "In the Cu/TEMPO oxidation, an aqueous EDTA wash (0.1 M) was added post-reaction, followed by a single liquid-liquid extraction with EtOAc. Copper levels fell below 1 ppm and isolated aldehyde yield increased from 78 % to 92 % without chromatography.": ["introduce_scavenging_step", "change_workup", "in_line_monitoring", "long_term_stability_test"],
    "A response-surface DoE varied HBr equivalents (4-8 eq) and water content (0-5 vol %). The optimum (8 eq HBr, 2 vol % water) gave >98 % conversion with no detectable intermediate. The same stoichiometry was transferred to a 100 kg batch with consistent results.": ["factorial_doe", "change_equivalents", "change_solvent", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A DoE screening was performed varying (i) oxidant equivalents (1.0-2.5 eq), (ii) catalyst loading (5-20 mol %), (iii) temperature profile (-10 °C -> rt vs. isothermal 25 °C), and (iv) solvent (DCM vs. toluene). The optimal condition (2.5 eq oxidant, 15 mol % catalyst, controlled-ramp) gave >= 95 % isolated yield on 150 g scale.": ["factorial_doe", "change_equivalents", "change_equivalents", "temperature_profile_study", "change_solvent", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Perform a factorial DoE varying (i) base identity (K₂CO₃, Na₂CO₃, K₃PO₄), (ii) solvent (acetone, MeCN, DMF, THF/H₂O), and (iii) electrophile equivalents (1.0-1.3 eq). Measure conversion at the target time; adopt the optimal set for a kilogram-scale run and verify that residual starting material falls below 2 %.": ["factorial_doe", "change_base", "change_solvent", "change_equivalents", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Perform a concentration series (5, 10, 20 mM) in a fixed-volume reactor while varying solvent (toluene, 1,2-DCE, MeCN) and temperature (80 °C vs 100 °C). Plot yield vs concentration to locate the breakpoint; adopt the optimal dilution or solvent that keeps yield >= 70 % at the target production concentration.": ["change_equivalents", "change_solvent", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A series of 3 L runs compared K₂CO₃ (3 eq) vs. KOt-Bu (1.5 eq) and temperatures of 70 °C vs. 85 °C. The combination of KOt-Bu and 85 °C gave >99 % conversion within 4 h, whereas the original K₂CO₃/70 °C protocol stalled at ~85 % conversion even after 12 h.": ["change_base", "change_equivalents", "temperature_profile_study", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A solvent-screening matrix compared pure toluene, toluene + 10 % MeOH, and pure MeOH as reaction media for the thionyl-chloride step. The toluene + 10 % MeOH system eliminated the emulsion, allowed smooth pumping, and maintained >90 % conversion. Inline phase-separator tests confirmed rapid disengagement.": ["change_solvent", "change_additive", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "in_line_monitoring", "long_term_stability_test"],
    "A pilot-scale flow reactor was fitted with a T-shaped static mixer and peristaltic pumps (instead of syringe pumps). The biphasic DCM/H₂O system was replaced by a homogeneous NMP/TEMPO system (solid-supported catalyst). Conversion rose from 55 % to > 95 % with stable pressure and no bubble-induced fluctuations.": ["change_reactor_configuration", "change_pumping_method", "change_solvent", "change_reagent_form", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "in_line_monitoring", "long_term_stability_test"],
    "Scale-up from 0.5 L to 10 L was tested with a conventional stirrer (ineffective) and then with an OBR (oscillatory baffled reactor). The OBR increased k_La by ~ 3-fold, reducing reaction time from 12 h to 45 min and giving consistent conversion.": ["change_reactor_configuration", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A solvent-screening matrix (EtOH, MeOH, PG, THF) identified 85 % EtOH/H₂O as fully miscible with the substrate and base. The optimal impeller geometry (low-shear pitched-blade) was installed in the CSTR, and the TBAOH/THF streams were fed via three synchronized pumps (16795). Scale-up runs showed no phase separation and > 95 % conversion.": ["change_solvent", "change_mixer_design", "change_pumping_method", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A solvent-screening matrix (DMA, MeCN, DMSO, 1,4-dioxane) was performed at 0.5 M substrate concentration. The best performance was achieved with DMA/MeCN (7:3 v/v), which dissolved both the aryl bromide and the aqueous base, eliminating the biphasic barrier and raising isolated yield from 45 % to 82 % on a 20 g scale.": ["change_solvent", "change_mixer_design", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A pressure-screen (1-5 bar) in a continuous oscillatory baffled reactor showed conversion of 3-butyn-2-ol rising from 60 % at 2 bar to >95 % at 5 bar, with selectivity retained when residence time was held constant (entry 7096). The optimal pressure was adopted for scale-up, and a back-pressure regulator prevented pressure spikes during hydrogen feed surges.": ["pressure_screen", "change_reactor_configuration", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Screened co-solvents (MeTHF, MeOH, MeCN) to achieve a homogeneous phase; the best result was 10 % v/v MeOH in THF, giving a single-phase slurry and full conversion in 2 h. Parallelly, a high-shear impeller was installed in a 200 L reactor, reducing the required residence time from 24 h to 6 h.": ["change_solvent", "change_mixer_design", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A DoE was run varying (i) the addition direction (substrate into acid vs. acid into substrate), (ii) the reactor temperature (-10 °C -> 0 °C) and (iii) the impeller type (standard vs. high-shear). The optimal condition was inverse addition of the substrate into a pre-cooled acid stream with a high-shear impeller, which eliminated clumps and gave >95 % conversion.":["factorial_doe", "addition_order_study", "temperature_profile_study", "change_mixer_design", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A high-shear Rushton turbine (4000 rpm) was installed in a 200 L reactor for the NCA-peptide coupling (entry 7111). Conversion rose from 61 % to 71 % and the slurry no longer adhered to the vessel wall. In parallel, adding 2 % TPGS-750-M surfactant (entry 2010) prevented agglomeration in aqueous Schotten-Baumann runs.":["change_mixer_design", "change_additive", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "- Test NBS solutions (e.g. 6 wt % in MeCN) versus solid addition in a 4 L reactor equipped with a downward-impeller stirrer at >= 800 rpm.  - Evaluate slurry-feed pumps for continuous dosing of bromine/NBS.  - Perform DoE on solvent/cosolvent ratios (MeCN/EtOAc, MeCN/DMSO) to achieve complete dissolution at the target concentration (~ 0.2 M).  - Scale to kilogram batch and monitor conversion uniformity by in-process sampling.":["change_reagent_form", "change_mixer_design", "factorial_doe", "change_solvent", "pilot_scale_validation", "in_line_monitoring"],
    "A DoE was run varying (i) base (NaOtBu -> DBU), (ii) solvent composition (toluene -> toluene/MeCN 1:1), and (iii) impeller speed (400 -> 800 rpm). Conversions were measured at 1 kg scale; the optimal combination (DBU, 1:1 MeCN/toluene, 800 rpm) gave >95 % conversion with a clear solution.":["factorial_doe", "change_base", "change_solvent", "change_mixer_design", "pilot_scale_validation", "in_line_monitoring"],
    "Conduct a DoE varying impeller speed (100 -> 1200 rpm) and solvent composition (e.g., adding 10 % v/v DMSO or NMP to the original aqueous/organic system). Measure slurry viscosity, conversion, and filtration time at pilot scale. Select the combination that yields a low-viscosity, fully mixed slurry with >= 95 % conversion.":["factorial_doe", "change_mixer_design", "change_solvent", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A pilot-scale study comparing three impeller types (Rushton turbine, pitched-blade, and helical ribbon) at 300 rpm, 600 rpm, and 900 rpm. Parallel runs were performed at 25 °C and 50 °C (the latter to reduce viscosity of NBP or N-butyl-pyrrolidinone). Mixing homogeneity was quantified by tracer dye dispersion time and conversion after 2 h.":["change_mixer_design", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A Design-of-Experiments (DoE) study varying agitation speed (100 - 500 rpm), impeller type (turbine vs. pitched-blade), and cosolvent % (5 % v/v DMSO, 10 % v/v MTBE). Reaction conversion and temperature profiles were monitored at 10 g L⁻¹ and 80 g L⁻¹ substrate loadings. The optimal condition (350 rpm, pitched-blade, 5 % v/v DMSO) restored >95 % conversion and eliminated emulsion formation.": ["factorial_doe", "change_mixer_design", "change_additive", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    '* Perform a solvent-screen (MeOH, EtOH, MeCN, THF, MeOH/THF 9:1) at constant acid loading, monitoring viscosity (rheometer) and conversion.  * Parallelly test mixing hardware: standard Rushton turbine vs. high-speed pitched-blade impeller in a 100 L jacketed reactor.  * In flow, compare a single-coil reactor vs. a modular train with inline static mixers. Choose the combination that yields < 10 % viscosity increase and >= 95 % conversion.': ["change_solvent", "change_mixer_design", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "* Perform a DoE screening of solvent/co-solvent ratios (e.g., EG : DMA, glycerol : EG) measuring torque on a pilot-scale agitator.  * Test a high-speed pitched-blade impeller versus a standard Rushton turbine at identical rpm.  * Evaluate residence-time distribution (RTD) in a flow loop with the new solvent system.": ["factorial_doe", "change_solvent", "change_mixer_design", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Screen a small solvent panel (e.g., IPA -> 2-MeTHF, MeCN -> acetone) at 1 L scale while measuring viscosity. If a solvent gives a clear solution, repeat the reaction with that solvent and a standard impeller; compare torque and filtration time.": ["change_solvent", "in_line_monitoring", "change_mixer_design", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A solvent-screen DoE (TBME, 2-MeTHF, MTBE) combined with base-equivalence screening (Na₂CO₃ 1 eq, NaHCO₃ 2.5 eq, no base) was run on a 30 L pilot. The optimal condition (2-MeTHF + NaHCO₃ 2.5 eq) gave a clear phase split and restored the 85 % isolated yield.": ["factorial_doe", "change_solvent", "change_base", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Screened solvents for pyrimidinone 3 (entries 4964/4966/4967) and identified sulfolane as fully dissolving both substrate and product. Implemented a 2 : 1 (v/v) 2-MeTHF/DME co-solvent system for the TMSCl-mediated chlorination (entry 7633) to achieve a stable biphasic mixture with Dₘ ~ 260. In flow, added a high-shear impeller to a 5 L stirred tank; slurry clearance time dropped from >30 min to <5 min, and residence-time distribution became uniform.": ["change_solvent", "change_additive", "change_mixer_design", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A solvent-screening DoE for the calcium-amide hydroamination replaced THF with DMA/DMF (1:1) and added 5 % water. The catalyst remained fully dissolved, conversion rose from 45 % (THF) to >90 % at identical temperature, and no slurry was observed on a 10 L scale.": ["factorial_doe", "change_solvent", "change_additive", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Screened cosolvents (IPA, MTBE, MeTHF, CPME) at 5 - 30 % v/v for the reduction of 2-chloro-1-(2,4-dichlorophenyl)-ethanone (entry 2398). 70 % v/v isopropanol gave >99 % conversion, whereas 10 % v/v gave only 68 %. For the fluoroketone DKR (entry 251), switching the work-up solvent from 2-MeTHF to EtOAc reduced product loss from 12 % to <3 %.": ["factorial_doe", "change_additive", "change_solvent", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "* Screen a solvent matrix (THF, MeCN, i-PrOH, CH₂Cl₂, water/MeCN) on 10 mmol scale, measuring solubility limits and conversion.  * Scale the best solvent to 1 kg, increase agitation speed, and monitor particle size distribution if a slurry remains.  * Implement the chosen solvent/co-solvent blend for pilot runs.": ["change_solvent", "factorial_doe", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A comparative run replaced solid NaBH₄ with a 1 M NaBH₄ solution in DMSO and introduced a controlled addition pump. Simultaneously, a temperature probe with a 30 °C interlock was installed. On a 5 kg scale the gas evolution was reduced to background levels, pressure stayed below 1 bar gauge, and isolated yield improved from 48 % to 71 %.": ["change_reagent_form", "change_pumping_method", "temperature_profile_study", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "The Ir-catalysed hydrogenation originally run at 5 barg was re-optimised with a more active Rh-BenzP* system, allowing operation at 1 atm H₂. A pressure-relief valve and automated vent-purge cycle were installed; no pressure excursions were observed in 100 h of continuous operation.": ["change_catalyst", "pressure_screen", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "long_term_stability_test"],
    "In the CDI-activated amide coupling (entry 21530) the addition of the amine was performed via a semi-batch feed over 30 min while maintaining a nitrogen headspace. The pressure stayed within 1 bar of the set-point and the reaction gave > 99 % conversion without venting issues.": ["addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A semi-batch addition of H₂O₂ over 4 h under a continuous N₂ blanket was tested in a 250 mL CSTR equipped with a pressure-relief valve. Inline O₂ sensor triggered automatic shutdown when O₂ > 2 % v/v. The modified protocol eliminated over-pressure events in kilogram-scale runs.": ["addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "- Install a PTFE-lined CSTR with a vented head-space and a downstream NaOH scrubber for HBr.  - Switch to a semi-batch addition where the organic substrate is added slowly to a pre-cooled Br₂/HBr mixture, keeping the temperature < 35 °C (as in entry 21151).  - Measure pressure transients with a pressure transducer; adjust feed rates until pressure rise stays below design limit (e.g., 0.5 bar).": ["change_reactor_configuration", "change_workup", "addition_order_study", "temperature_profile_study", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A comparative run substituted Cbz-Cl with Fmoc-Cl (lower HCl release) and introduced pyridine (2 eq) as an HCl scavenger. Gas-flow meters showed a >90 % reduction in HCl evolution, and the reaction proceeded with identical conversion.": ["change_substrate", "introduce_scavenging_step", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Installed a 8 bar back-pressure regulator on the EtOAc flow coil (α-thioamide/NCS cascade) and a sealed Hastelloy autoclave for POCl₃-mediated chlorinations. Added a drying/scrubbing bottle (conc. H₂SO₄) upstream of the reactor for Cl₂ feeds. Measured pressure profiles before and after; pressure excursions were eliminated and gas-liquid mass transfer improved, giving >85 % conversion.": ["change_reactor_configuration", "change_workup", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A scale-up trial in a 10 L stainless-steel reactor equipped with a calibrated pressure transducer. The thionyl-chloride feed was split into three equal portions over 30 min (vs a single charge). Gas-scrubbing with aqueous NaHCO₃ was installed on the vent line. Pressure profiles, gas composition (by FTIR), and conversion were recorded. A parallel run used a continuous-flow microreactor with a back-pressure regulator set to 1 bar.": ["addition_order_study", "change_workup", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A DoE varying inlet temperature, feed-pump ramp-rate, and reactor headspace pressure was run on a pilot-scale packed-bed (Raney Ni 3111A). An external FLIR camera replaced the invasive temperature probe (see entry 20354) to avoid channeling. The optimal condition (inlet 36 °C, slow pump ramp, stainless-steel reactor with PTFE liner) eliminated pressure spikes in three consecutive 2-h runs.": ["factorial_doe", "change_reactor_configuration", "change_mixer_design", "temperature_profile_study", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "* Run the deprotection in a pilot-scale batch reactor equipped with a pressure-rated vent line and a back-pressure regulator set at 5 bar.  * Measure pressure profiles with and without a gas-sparge (N₂) and with different residence times.  * In flow, compare a stainless-steel coil (high surface-to-volume) vs. a PFA coil at identical temperature, monitoring pressure and temperature spikes.  * Select the configuration that keeps pressure < 6 bar and temperature deviation < 2 °C.": ["change_reactor_configuration", "addition_order_study", "temperature_profile_study", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "* Conduct a small-scale kinetic study varying the addition rate of the dithionite (or other gas-forming reagent) while monitoring pressure in a sealed, instrumented reactor.  * Install a vent line with a scrubber and test different vent-flow rates.  * Compare batch vs. continuous-flow operation with a static-mixing segment that shortens residence time of the gas-rich zone.": ["addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "change_reactor_configuration", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Run the reaction in three configurations: (i) sealed batch, (ii) batch with a 400 Torr vacuum, (iii) continuous N₂ sweep at 0.2 L min⁻¹. Record pressure profiles, ethylene concentration in the headspace, and product yield. Choose the configuration that maintains steady pressure and maximises conversion.": ["change_reactor_configuration", "addition_order_study", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Added a vent or back-pressure regulator set to a safe limit; introduced inert gas sparging to dilute reactive gases; reduced the amount of gas-forming reagent or changed to a less gas-intensive oxidant/reductant.": ["change_reactor_configuration", "addition_order_study", "change_oxidant", "pressure_drop_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A side-by-side comparison was performed: (A) Na(OAc)₃BH at 5 °C for 24 h (baseline) vs. (B) 2-picoline.BH₃ at 50 °C for 1 h. The flow version of (B) used a three-stage plug-flow reactor with 1 min residence per stage. Conversion rose from 70 % to > 99 % and overall throughput increased 12-fold.": ["change_reductant", "temperature_profile_study", "change_reactor_configuration", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A DoE varying catalyst loading (0.2 -> 0.8 mol %), temperature (80 -> 110 °C), and ligand (Xantphos -> tBuXPhos) was performed on the copper-catalysed amination of 6-bromoquinoline. The optimal condition (0.5 mol % Cu, 110 °C, tBuXPhos) reduced reaction time from 48 h to 6 h while maintaining >92 % isolated yield.": ["factorial_doe", "change_equivalents", "temperature_profile_study", "change_ligand", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Moved the step to continuous flow with higher temperature or pressure to accelerate kinetics; increased temperature within safety limits; shortened residence time after kinetic modeling.": ["change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "kinetic_modeling", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A DoE screening of agitation speed (250 -> 600 rpm), addition mode (single-charge solid vs. split-charge solution), and solvent (2-propanol, MeCN, EtOAc) was performed on a 10 g pilot reactor. The optimal condition combined a 600 rpm impeller, three equal portions of a 1 M NaBH(OAc)₃ solution in EtOAc, and a co-solvent (MeCN) that kept the amine fully dissolved. Conversion rose from 45 % to > 95 % with no visible solids.": ["factorial_doe", "change_mixer_design", "addition_order_study", "change_solvent", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Screen a small DoE of solvents (e.g., THF/H₂O, toluene/water, MeCN/H₂O) and base particle size (200 mesh vs. 325 mesh). Select the combination that gives a clear homogeneous reaction at the target temperature, then run a pilot-scale batch with a high-speed impeller (>=300 rpm) and monitor temperature uniformity and conversion.": ["factorial_doe", "change_solvent", "change_particle_size", "change_mixer_design", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A DoE screening of impeller type (Rushton vs. pitched-blade) and agitation speed was performed on a 10 L reactor; simultaneously, a 10 % v/v THF co-solvent was added to the DMA/K₂CO₃ system. Parallel runs in a continuous-flow tube with a static-mixing element were also evaluated. The optimal condition (high-speed pitched-blade + 10 % THF) gave quantitative conversion and uniform temperature profiles.": ["factorial_doe", "change_mixer_design", "change_solvent", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A Kenics static mixer was installed in the feed line of the HDIT/MEKO reaction; the HDIT feed was pre-heated to 75 °C to drop viscosity below 500 mPa.s. The slurry remained fluid, temperature remained uniform, and conversion reached >95 % with no pressure drop.": ["change_reactor_configuration", "change_mixer_design", "change_solvent", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"], 
    "Replaced IPA (~ 50 vol %) with isopropyl acetate (10 vol %) and added a small amount of isopropanol to lower viscosity (Symptom 2). A controlled cooling crystallisation (40 °C -> 15 °C) was introduced to precipitate the product as a filterable solid, reducing filtration pressure by 70 %.": ["change_solvent", "change_additive", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Screen a set of solvents (THF, MeCN, 2-MeTHF) and bases (K₂CO₃, DBU, t-BuTMG) in small-scale reactors; measure slurry formation (visual inspection, torque) and conversion. Implement the best-performing solvent/base pair and a high-shear impeller in a pilot-scale batch, confirming the absence of slurry and consistent conversion.": ["change_solvent", "change_base", "change_mixer_design", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A DoE screening of solvent/co-solvent combinations (DMAc, MeCN, IPA, water) and particle-size grading of K₂CO₃ was performed; high-shear impellers and staged addition of the nucleophile were evaluated on a 50 L pilot reactor. The optimal condition used MeCN + 1 % water with finely milled K₂CO₃ and a 3 h controlled feed, giving a clear, single-phase slurry and consistent conversion.": ["factorial_doe", "change_solvent", "change_particle_size", "change_mixer_design", "addition_order_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Switched to a solvent (or co-solvent) that keeps all components in solution; reduced solid loading; added a small amount of a polar co-solvent or surfactant; upgraded impeller to a high-shear design.": ["change_solvent", "change_additive", "change_mixer_design", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A series of temperature-ramp studies were performed in a jacketed reactor: (i) pre-cool the acid stream to -10 °C, (ii) add the substrate over 30 min with a controlled ramp, (iii) install a high-efficiency coil heat-exchanger. The temperature excursion was limited to <2 °C and the epimerisation impurity dropped from 0.3 % to <0.05 %.": ["temperature_profile_study", "addition_order_study", "change_mixer_design", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A calorimetric study (DSC) defined the maximum adiabatic temperature rise. The batch reactor was equipped with a double-jacket heat exchanger and a semi-batch H₂O₂ feed (0.5 mL min⁻¹) controlled by a PID loop. Temperature was held <= 30 °C throughout a 200 g run, eliminating runaway.": ["change_reactor_configuration", "addition_order_study", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A temperature-ramp study added NaBH(OAc)₃ over 50 min while maintaining the reactor at 17 °C (instead of 25 °C). A stainless-steel jacket with a 5 °C coolant inlet was installed. The maximum temperature rise was limited to 5 °C, and the isolated yield increased from 48 % to 69 % with no impurity formation.": ["temperature_profile_study", "addition_order_study", "change_reactor_configuration", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A DoE on temperature-ramp rate and external coolant flow was performed in a 5 L autoclave; the optimal ramp (2 °C min⁻¹) and a downstream heat-exchanger kept the temperature <= 30 °C above set-point, eliminating hot-spots and preserving product purity.": ["factorial_doe", "temperature_profile_study", "change_reactor_configuration", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A DoE on feed-rate, inlet temperature and cooling-jacket flow was performed on a pilot-scale reactor. The optimal condition kept the residence time at 7 min, used a 0 °C inlet slurry and a cooling-jacket set-point of 2 °C. Temperature excursions were limited to <= 1 °C and conversion remained > 90 %.": ["factorial_doe", "addition_order_study", "temperature_profile_study", "change_reactor_configuration", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A DoE on temperature-ramp profiles was performed: (i) reduce the maximum reaction temperature from 240 °C to 130 °C (11051), (ii) implement a semi-batch addition of LiOH/H₂O₂ over 4 h while maintaining 25 °C (16796), and (iii) install a high-efficiency coil-in-jacket and monitor temperature with a fast-response RTD. The optimized conditions eliminated temperature overshoot in pilot-scale runs.": ["factorial_doe", "temperature_profile_study", "addition_order_study", "change_reactor_configuration", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "- Conduct calorimetric studies to quantify the heat-release profile.  - Implement semi-batch feeding of bromine/NBS (e.g. 5-10 min aliquots) while actively cooling with a jacket capable of >= 2 kW removal.  - Verify temperature stability with in-line thermocouples; repeat at pilot-scale (~ 100 kg) to confirm no temperature excursions > 5 °C.": ["addition_order_study", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A calorimetric study quantified the heat of reaction (-135 kJ mol⁻¹). The batch reactor was equipped with a jacket capable of 5 kW cooling. A ramp from 0 °C to 25 °C over 2 h was programmed before holding at 50 °C. Temperature spikes were eliminated, and product purity improved from 92 % to >98 % with no Pd black formation.": ["change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Design a semi-batch addition study: feed the bromide substrate over 30 min while monitoring reactor temperature with an inline probe. Compare continuous addition, split-charge, and slow-drip addition. Install a jacketed reactor with a high-capacity coolant and validate that the temperature never exceeds the safety limit (e.g., 45 °C). Scale the optimized addition profile to kilogram scale and confirm reproducible temperature control.": ["addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    
    "Perform calorimetry on a small scale to obtain ΔH and adiabatic temperature rise; then implement a staged addition (pre-cool reagents, semi-batch feed) and/or upgrade jacket/heat-exchanger capacity; monitor temperature with fast-response probes.": ["addition_order_study", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    
    "A semi-batch addition profile was programmed: the exothermic reagent was fed over 2 h while the reactor temperature was held at 5 °C (jacket). Parallel flow experiments used a 0.5 L PFR with a 30 s residence time and a 0 °C jacket. Both approaches kept the bulk temperature <=10 °C and eliminated product degradation.": ["addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Implement a semi-batch feed where the amine solution is added over 30 min while monitoring temperature with an inline probe. Compare a standard addition (instant) versus a ramped addition (0 -> 30 min) and evaluate conversion, impurity profile, and temperature excursions. If needed, install a higher-capacity heat-exchanger and repeat the test.": ["addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Performed a DoE on addition temperature, addition rate, and jacket coolant flow. Implemented a syringe-pump addition of POCl₃ (or SO₂Cl₂) over 15 min while maintaining the reactor at -20 °C (or <=40 °C for POCl₃). In parallel, installed a high-efficiency jacket with internal coils (for batch) and a 0.030 in. PFA coil with 75 psi back-pressure (for flow). Monitored adiabatic temperature rise with calorimetry; the maximum ΔT dropped from >100 °C to <5 °C.": ["factorial_doe", "addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A design-of-experiments (DoE) study varied acid addition rate (dropwise vs. pump), jacket temperature, and quench temperature. The optimal condition was a controlled acid feed (<= 0.5 m L min⁻¹) into a jacket-cooled reactor (10 °C set-point), which limited the temperature spike to < 3 °C and eliminated product degradation.": ["factorial_doe", "addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A temperature-screen (10 °C -> 75 °C) with constant base loading identified 30 °C as the threshold below which racemisation of the α-chiral ester was < 1 % ee loss. The process was then transferred to a jacket-cooled flow reactor maintaining 28 °C, achieving > 99 % ee at production scale.": ["temperature_profile_study", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A Design-of-Experiments (DoE) study varying (i) addition rate of the most exothermic reagent (e.g., benzoyl chloride, thionyl chloride, dimethyl sulfate), (ii) reaction temperature set-point (0 °C -> 30 °C), and (iii) catalyst choice (Fe(OTf)₂ vs H₂SO₄). Each condition was run in a 5 L jacketed reactor equipped with a calibrated PID controller and external heat-exchange coils. Temperature profiles, conversion, and impurity levels were recorded.": ["factorial_doe", "addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "change_catalyst", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A controlled-addition study using a syringe pump to deliver the amine over 45 min at 5 °C while the reactor was jacketed at 0 °C (entry 964). Temperature was logged with an external probe; the peak rise was limited to 2 °C versus >12 °C in the batch addition. Product impurity F fell below detection, and yield improved by 8 %.": ["addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A calorimetric study measured the adiabatic temperature rise for NaBH₄ addition to ketone 13. The addition was split into four equal portions over 30 min while the reactor jacket maintained 0 °C. Temperature was kept <=5 °C throughout, eliminating product degradation. Parallel runs with Na-selectride showed that switching to K-selectride (same stoichiometry) reduced the peak temperature by ~8 °C.": ["addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "change_reductant", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "* Implement a split-addition protocol (three equal portions over 30 min) while measuring temperature with an inline thermocouple.  * Install a jacketed reactor with a PID-controlled coolant loop; compare temperature profiles with and without the jacket.  * Use calorimetric data to calculate the adiabatic temperature rise and size the cooling duty accordingly.": ["addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study","in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Perform a DoE on addition rate, cooling-jacket flow, and inlet temperature; monitor temperature profiles in a pilot-scale reactor. If the peak exceeds the safety limit, test a less-exothermic reagent (e.g., replace HBr with HCl, Et₂O with THF, or switch to a milder oxidant).": ["factorial_doe", "addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "change_oxidant", "change_solvent", "change_acid", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "* Perform a calorimetric study of the exothermic addition on 100 g scale to determine heat-of-reaction (kJ mol⁻¹).  * Design a semi-batch feed (e.g., DPPA added over 2 h at 13-17 °C) and test on 1 kg with a jacketed reactor equipped with a coil.  * Record temperature profiles and compare conversion/ee to a fast-addition run.": ["addition_order_study", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Design a DoE varying (i) addition rate (slow vs fast), (ii) feed-line temperature (ambient vs -20 °C), and (iii) jacket set-point (± 5 °C). Monitor temperature profiles, conversion, and impurity formation. Select the combination that keeps the temperature rise < 5 °C and restores yield.": ["factorial_doe", "addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Calorimetric (ARC) profiling identified the adiabatic temperature rise. A staged, syringe-pump addition of the electrophile over 30 mL h⁻¹ was introduced, and the reactor jacket temperature was limited to 95 °C (vs. 120 °C in the original). A high-efficiency coil heat-exchanger was installed for rapid quench. The modified protocol eliminated temperature excursions (> 2 °C) on a 200 kg batch.": ["addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Implemented active cooling (jacket, ice-bath) and split the addition into multiple, temperature-controlled portions; in some cases a new reactor with high-efficiency heat-exchange channels was installed.": ["change_reactor_configuration", "addition_order_study", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A controlled semi-batch feeding protocol (10 % of amine added every 5 min) was programmed on a 5 L reactor, and an inline UV-vis probe monitored imine concentration. Stoichiometry was tightened to 1.3 equiv amine. Yield reproducibility improved from a 15 % spread to < 2 % spread over ten consecutive runs.": ["addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "An online GC-FID was installed on a 15 L hydrogenation loop; data were fed into a digital twin that adjusted H₂ flow to maintain a constant dissolved H₂ concentration. Over 30 runs the conversion CV dropped from ± 12 % to ± 3 %.": ["in_line_monitoring", "change_reactor_configuration", "change_pumping_method", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "- Perform a small-scale qualification test for each new NBS lot (e.g., 5 g reaction, monitor conversion).  - Use kinetic modeling to define a conservative NBS equivalence (e.g., 1.40 eq) that ensures > 98 % conversion for both high- and low-Br₂ batches.  - Add 5 mol % citric-acid (or NTA/EDTA) to chelate trace Cu that slows photobromination.  - Document acceptance criteria and implement a lot-release protocol.": ["introduce_scavenging_step", "kinetic_modeling", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A scale-up (200 kg) was performed in a 500 L stainless reactor. Prior to charge, the vessel was sparged three times with nitrogen and then sealed. An inline dissolved-oxygen probe was installed; O₂ was kept <5 ppm. Conversion improved from 70 % (no purge) to >95 % with the purge protocol.": ["change_reactor_configuration", "introduce_scavenging_step", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A catalyst-loading DoE (0.25 mol % -> 0.75 mol %) was performed on a 5 g scale using the Rh-Segphos system. The ethylene-Rh precursor gave consistent conversion (~80 %) across the loading range, whereas the original RhCl₂ dimer showed > 30 % spread. The optimized loading (0.5 mol %) was adopted for all subsequent scales.": ["factorial_doe", "change_equivalents", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Implemented a split-charge addition for NCS in the α-thioamide flow cascade (entries 15573/15574/15575). Compared single-charge (<=30 % conversion) vs. three-portion addition (>=85 % conversion). For DCDMH chlorinations (entries 1374/1375) introduced a three-portion, -5 °C addition, which reduced the des-TMS impurity from 5 % to <=0.2 %. Conducted a DoE varying feed ratio and temperature, confirming optimal NCS equivalents of 2.05-2.1 equiv.": ["addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Conduct a Design-of-Experiments varying cooling rate (0.1-1 °C min⁻¹), antisolvent addition rate (4-20 mL min⁻¹), and seed loading (0.5-5 wt %). Use in-line Raman or FBRM to monitor nucleation events and select the region that yields a narrow PSD and target polymorph.": ["factorial_doe", "change_additive", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "* Conduct a small DoE varying base equivalents (0.95-1.10 eq) and temperature ramp profiles (20 °C -> 50 °C vs. isothermal).  * Measure conversion at 5 min, 15 min, 30 min on 100 g and 5 kg batches.  * Select the combination that gives <2 % conversion spread; lock the base loading in the kinetic model.": ["factorial_doe", "change_base", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "Performed a Design-of-Experiments (DoE) to tighten stoichiometric windows; introduced a staged addition (e.g., add base after substrate is fully dissolved); installed real-time temperature/pH control loops.": ["factorial_doe", "change_base", "addition_order_study", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
    "A controlled-feed study was carried out: the hydrazone was delivered over 3 h via a syringe pump into a jacketed 25 L reactor held at 25 °C. An external cooling loop maintained the bulk temperature within ±2 °C. The temperature spike was eliminated, conversion rose to 94 % and no catalyst decomposition was observed.": ["addition_order_study", "change_pumping_method", "change_reactor_configuration", "temperature_profile_study", "in_line_monitoring", "pilot_scale_validation"],
}


